# Generated per-run artefacts under results/ are ignored by default...
results/

# ...but the Kimi K3 provenance chain REQUIRES its results to be committable.
# check_reference_lock.py (the `lock` CI job) refuses any non-zero baseline in
# reference.lock unless a bench/results JSON records the same node and context. With
# results/ blanket-ignored, that JSON could only be committed with `git add -f`, so
# the provenance rule was unsatisfiable in normal use and the pins could never be
# filled legitimately. Un-ignore exactly what the K3 harness emits.
!results/
results/*
!results/kimi_k3_*.json
!results/kimi_k3_*.md
!results/tp_*.md
!results/accuracy_*.md
!results/qwen3-*.md

!competitors/results/
!competitors/results/qwen3_awq_rtx5090_20260703/
!competitors/results/qwen3_awq_rtx5090_20260703/**
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.venv/
